#
# Minimal direwolf.conf for the Checkpoint Pi bridge.
#
# Reference: https://github.com/wb2osz/direwolf/blob/master/doc/User-Guide.pdf
#
# Copy this to ~/.direwolf.conf (or wherever your install expects), edit the
# callsign and audio device, then run: direwolf -t 0
#

#
# Audio device. ADEVICE accepts ALSA device names (Linux), CoreAudio device
# names (macOS), or a sound-card index. Use `arecord -L` (Linux) to discover.
#
ADEVICE plughw:1,0

ACHANNELS 1

#
# Channel-0 config. MYCALL must be your licensed callsign with the SSID you've
# allocated to this checkpoint. AJ6UU-1 through AJ6UU-15 are typical for a
# multi-checkpoint event; -10 is conventionally an iGate, so prefer 1..9 for
# checkpoint bridges.
#
CHANNEL 0
MYCALL AJ6UU-1
MODEM 1200
# Push-to-talk: GPIO 23 on a Pi with a PTT cable, RIG <N> for hamlib CAT,
# or omit entirely if the radio uses VOX.
PTT GPIO 23

#
# KISS-over-TCP. The bridge talks to direwolf here.
# Leave the AGW port (KISSPORT/AGWPORT) defaults unless you have a reason.
#
KISSPORT 8001

#
# Stop direwolf from doing things on its own — we are the application.
# Comment out IGSERVER if you DO want this Pi to also act as an iGate.
#
# IGSERVER noam.aprs2.net
# IGLOGIN AJ6UU 12345
